Client code should be shielded from how settings specific to an environment are injected
as this mechanism might change.

The "environment" package provides abstraction for settings and all their sources to evolve
independently from clients like k8s extensions or operators. Environment here should be understood
as least common denominator across any consumers. Ideally the package resides in a common golang
library shared between consumers like k8s extensions and operators. Most environment setting
influence how clients interact with Prism, like which credentials to use. Hence prism-go-client can serve as common golang library.

Moreover multiple clients like Kubernetes clusters might share certain properties of an environment
like the categories and project. However idea is that each k8s cluster environment is unique to
allow infrastructure resources created on behalf of a k8s cluster to be associated with this particular k8s cluster.

We envision the following sources for environment settings:

1. "Local" using OS environment variables as source
2. "SecretDir" expecting k8s secret to be mounted as directory into container
3. "ConfigMap" expecting k8s config map to b mounted as directory into container
4. "Kubernetes" expecting access to k8s via informers for reading secrets directly

Following is the interface through which environment is accessed.

```
// Environment in which a Kubernetes has been deployed.
type Environment interface {
	// GetManagementEndpoint retrieves managment endpoint
	GetManagementEndpoint(topology Topology) (*ManagementEndpoint, error)
	// Get retrieves settings applicable to the environment like project
	// or category to which resources created on behalf of Kubernetes cluster are
	// assigned to.
	// These settings might have to be explicitly propagated to resources.
	// Return whether lookup was successful to distinguish from nil as value.
	Get(topology Topology, key string) (interface{}, error)
}
```

The same interface is implemented by all environment sources/providers.

## Overview
Change scala Amap to Rholang Amap in compiler.
Separate local map and state.
## Results
Lmap declaration:
```scala
new LMap, state in {
  contract LMap(return, @"decl") = {
    new INP, OUTP, ORT02, LIFNR in {
      state!({"INP":*INP, "OUTP":*OUTP, "ORT02":*ORT02, "LIFNR":*LIFNR}) |
      for(_ <<- state) {return!(true)}
    }
  } |
  contract LMap(return, @"get", @field) = {
    for(@s <<- state) {
      let chan <- s.get(field) in {
        for(x <<- chan) {return!(*x)}
      }
    }    
  } |
  contract LMap(return, @"update", @field, @value) = {
    for(@s <<- state) {
      let chan <- s.get(field) in {
        for(_ <- chan) {chan!(value) | for(_ <<- chan) {return!(true)}}
      }
    }
  }
}
```
LMap initialization:
```scala
contract localInit(ret0, l) = {
  for(_ <- l!?("update", "INP", "")) {
    for(_ <- l!?("update", "OUTP", "")) {
      for(_ <- l!?("update", "ORT02", "")) {
        for(_ <- l!?("update", "LIFNR", "")) {
          ret0!(true)
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
ProcessRecord contract:
```scala
contract processRecord(return, s, l, @(recKey, recValues)) = {
  new processField, saveRecordDataLoop, processFieldLoop in {    
    contract processField(ret, @fieldName) = {
      new BELNR, RECIPNT_NO, IDDAT, PARVW, IDDAT_colon_4, QUALF_colon_2, TEMP_IDTNR_colon_3 in {
        contract BELNR(ret0) = {
          for(@val_current_BELNR <- s!?("get", recKey, "BELNR")) {
            for(_ <- l!?("update", "INP", val_current_BELNR)) {
              for(@val_local_INP <- l!?("get", "INP")) {
                for(_ <- l!?("update", "OUTP", val_local_INP.slice(2, (2 + 8)))) {
                  for(@val_local_OUTP <- l!?("get", "OUTP")) {
                    for(_ <- s!?("update", recKey, "BELNR", val_local_OUTP)) {
                      ret0!(true)
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        } |
        contract RECIPNT_NO(ret0) = {
          for(@val_current_RECIPNT_NO <- s!?("get", recKey, "RECIPNT_NO")) {
            for(_ <- s!?("update", recKey, "RECIPNT_NO", val_current_RECIPNT_NO.slice(((val_current_RECIPNT_NO.length() - 1) - 8), (val_current_RECIPNT_NO.length() - 1)))) {
              ret0!(true)
            }
          }
        } |
        contract IDDAT(ret0) = {
          for(@val_current_IDDAT <- s!?("get", recKey, "IDDAT")) {
            new ret1 in {
              if(val_current_IDDAT == "012") {
                for(@val_current_DATUM_colon_3 <- s!?("get", recKey, "DATUM_colon_3")) {
                  for(_ <- s!?("update", "CLAIM3N", "DATUM_colon_4", val_current_DATUM_colon_3)) {
                    ret1!(true)
                  }
                }
              }
              else {
                ret1!(true)
              } |
              for(_<-ret1) {
                ret0!(true)
              }
            }
          }
        } |
        contract PARVW(ret0) = {
          for(@val_current_PARVW <- s!?("get", recKey, "PARVW")) {
            new ret1 in {
              if(val_current_PARVW == "WE") {
                for(@val_current_ORT02_colon_3 <- s!?("get", recKey, "ORT02_colon_3")) {
                  for(_ <- s!?("update", "CLAIM3N", "TEMP_ORT02", val_current_ORT02_colon_3)) {
                    ret1!(true)
                  }
                }
              }
              else {
                ret1!(true)
              } |
              for(_<-ret1) {
                ret0!(true)
              }
            }
          }
        } |
        contract IDDAT_colon_4(ret0) = {
          for(@val_current_IDDAT_colon_4 <- s!?("get", recKey, "IDDAT_colon_4")) {
            new ret1 in {
              if(val_current_IDDAT_colon_4 == "032") {
                for(@val_current_DATUM_colon_2 <- s!?("get", recKey, "DATUM_colon_2")) {
                  for(_ <- s!?("update", "E2EDP01", "DATUM_colon_3", val_current_DATUM_colon_2)) {
                    ret1!(true)
                  }
                }
              }
              else {
                ret1!(true)
              } |
              for(_<-ret1) {
                ret0!(true)
              }
            }
          }
        } |
        contract QUALF_colon_2(ret0) = {
          for(@val_current_QUALF_colon_2 <- s!?("get", recKey, "QUALF_colon_2")) {
            new ret1 in {
              if(val_current_QUALF_colon_2 == "003") {
                for(@val_current_IDTNR <- s!?("get", recKey, "IDTNR")) {
                  for(_ <- s!?("update", "E2EDP01", "TEMP_IDTNR", val_current_IDTNR)) {
                    for(@val_current_IDTNR <- s!?("get", recKey, "IDTNR")) {
                      for(_ <- s!?("update", "E2EDP01", "TEMP_IDTNR_colon_4", val_current_IDTNR.slice(11, (11 + 1)))) {
                        ret1!(true)
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
              else {
                ret1!(true)
              } |
              for(_<-ret1) {
                for(@val_current_QUALF_colon_2 <- s!?("get", recKey, "QUALF_colon_2")) {
                  new ret1 in {
                    if(val_current_QUALF_colon_2 == "007") {
                      for(@val_current_IDTNR <- s!?("get", recKey, "IDTNR")) {
                        for(_ <- s!?("update", "E2EDP01", "TEMP_IDTNR_colon_2", val_current_IDTNR)) {
                          for(@val_current_MFRNR <- s!?("get", recKey, "MFRNR")) {
                            for(_ <- s!?("update", "E2EDP01", "TEMP_IDTNR_colon_3", val_current_MFRNR)) {
                              ret1!(true)
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                    else {
                      ret1!(true)
                    } |
                    for(_<-ret1) {
                      ret0!(true)
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        } |
        contract TEMP_IDTNR_colon_3(ret0) = {
          ret0!(true)
        } |
        match fieldName {
          "BELNR" => { for(@res <- BELNR!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          "RECIPNT_NO" => { for(@res <- RECIPNT_NO!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          "IDDAT" => { for(@res <- IDDAT!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          "PARVW" => { for(@res <- PARVW!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          "IDDAT_colon_4" => { for(@res <- IDDAT_colon_4!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          "QUALF_colon_2" => { for(@res <- QUALF_colon_2!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          "TEMP_IDTNR_colon_3" => { for(@res <- TEMP_IDTNR_colon_3!?()) { ret!(res) } }
          _ => ret!(true)
        }
      }
    } |
    contract processFieldLoop(@keys) = {
      match keys {
        Set(head... tail) => {
          for(_ <- processField!?(head)) { processFieldLoop!(tail) }
        }
        _ => { return!(true) }
      }
    } |
    contract saveRecordDataLoop(@KVs) = {
      match KVs {
        [head... tail] => {
          for(_ <- s!?("update", recKey, head.nth(0), head.nth(1))) {
            saveRecordDataLoop!(tail)
          }
        }
        _ => { processFieldLoop!(recValues.keys()) }
      }
    } |
    saveRecordDataLoop!(recValues.toList())
  }
}
```
